# Agent worktrees. MUST stay ignored: a worktree directory that is tracked gets
# committed as a gitlink (mode 160000). That already happened once —
# `.claude/worktrees/platform-neutral` was committed in 3b2cc9d and had to be
# stripped during the SHA-256 -> SHA-1 conversion, because a gitlink's object id
# cannot be remapped across hash algorithms. (`3b2cc9d` is the SHA-1 id; the
# gitlink itself is no longer visible there, because the conversion stripped it —
# it survives only in the archived GitLab project.)
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions. Untracked deliberately: `settings.local.json`
# is personal, per-machine state — it held one developer's exact pool/wallet
# command line and showed as modified in every `git status` for the life of the
# project. Shared, reviewable settings belong in `.claude/settings.json`, which
# stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# cargo-mutants scratch. Untracked deliberately, for two reasons found
# independently one PR apart: volume and disclosure. Every run writes ~788 KB
# and rotates the previous directory to mutants.out.old, so a documented
# invocation dirties dozens of files — PR #24 committed 102 of them. And
# `lock.json` records the operator's hostname, username and absolute home paths,
# which PR #23 swept in via a `git add -A` (25 files, 5.7 MB) into a **public**
# repository. Both directories are listed because a run creates both. The
# findings belong in `AUDIT.md`; the directories are scratch.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Review ledgers written by independent reviewer agents during review. These are
# **deliberately ignored** to close the accidental path — `git add -A` can then
# never sweep them in (that command committed mutants.out/ to the public repo
# this month). Committing a ledger is still *possible* and still *intended* (the
# rules at `.claude/agents/_shared-context.md` rules 1-3 say to commit as you
# go, for crash recovery), but requires `git add -f`. A CI check fails if a ledger
# reaches the PR, so the deliberate path is gated at merge time too. See LEDGER-01
# and PROC-07 in AUDIT.md for the history and justification.
REVIEW_*.md
